# PR-archive shard store: a MACHINE-WRITTEN data store, not authored source
# (081KZYMY46P087G0R003S64V2B). One file per archived PR (~6.3k files today, one more per
# merge), each emitted by `pr-manifest-shards.ts` as canonical `JSON.stringify(…, 2)` bytes.
# Two reasons it is excluded rather than formatted: prettier collapses short `source_ids`
# arrays onto one line, which would put the FORMATTER and the GENERATOR in a permanent fight
# (the generator must reproduce the checked-in bytes — that is what makes the derived
# manifest a drift gate); and `--check` over the store costs ~30 s of CI for zero review
# value on files no human hand-edits. Same stance as the `artifacts/` entries above.
docs/github/prs/shards/

# Website-traveler style boundary: a website is its own traveler with its own
# traditional style/CSS at its own boundary — NOT enforced by Zeta's tooling
# (the style/CSS inversion, Aaron 2026-06-10). Excludes the website's CSS from
# prettier (stylelint excludes it too via .stylelintignore).
full-ai-cluster/portal/web/**/*.css

# Generated currency report (`report-chart-currency.ts --write`). MACHINE-WRITTEN,
# never hand-edited, and its whole value is that re-running the generator reproduces
# the checked-in bytes — that byte-match is what makes `--check` a drift signal and
# what stops a weekly job dirtying the tree. Prettier re-pads markdown table cells and
# rewrites `*em*` to `_em_`, which would put the FORMATTER and the GENERATOR in a
# permanent fight over the same file, exactly as with `docs/github/prs/shards/` above.
# The generator, not prettier, owns these bytes.
docs/CHART-CURRENCY.md

# VERBATIM COPIES OF GIT HISTORY. The four pre-fix `Application.yaml` files under
# `testdata/inert-valuesobject-history/` are byte-for-byte `git show <sha>:<path>`
# output, and `inert-valuesobject-keys.test.ts` re-verifies them against those very
# objects. Formatting them would break that verification for the sake of tidying a
# manifest nobody will ever deploy — and would leave the guard's four falsifiers
# resting on files the repository could no longer confirm are the real history.
# The commits, not prettier, own these bytes.
src/Core.TypeScript/cluster/testdata/inert-valuesobject-history/*.yaml

# Git-native inverted index: a MACHINE-WRITTEN artifact, not authored source
# (081M0QTXTR3087G0R002R439FH). Rebuilt from an explicit git rev every ~6 hours by
# `search-index-cadence.yml`, and its defining property is that rebuilding at the
# same rev produces BYTE-IDENTICAL files (discipline #6, and the reason its diffs
# are meaningful at all). Prettier would reformat the generator's output and put
# the FORMATTER and the GENERATOR in a permanent fight — the same reason
# docs/github/prs/ is excluded above. `renderTermRow` pins the exact bytes.
db/search-index/
